  "body": {
    "id": "thm:minimax-width-frontier",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "There exist constants \\(0<c<C<\\infty\\) such that \\(c r_n\\le\\mathfrak R_n\\le C r_n\\) for all sufficiently large \\(n\\); equivalently, \\(\\mathfrak R_n\\asymp\\{\\log\\log n/\\log n\\}^{\\beta-1/2}\\).",
    "free_symbols": [
      "\\(r_n\\)",
      "\\(\\mathfrak R_n\\)",
      "\\(n\\)",
      "\\(\\beta\\)"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "thm:honest-upper-band",
      "thm:fixed-nuisance-marked-pair",
      "def:honest-band-class"
    ],
    "justification": "The matching expected-maximal-width frontier is the theorem-level statistical contribution and holds throughout the Sobolev embedding range \\(\\beta>1/2\\).",
    "gap": "No cited work matches a witness-certified honest ADRF sup-band upper bound to a fixed-nuisance marked lower bound under fully blind asymmetric replicates with spectral zeros.",
    "consumer": "Study designers can translate the frontier into sample-size calculations for resolving dose-response features.",
    "proof_tex": "The repaired upper-band theorem supplies one data-driven member of \\(\\mathfrak B_{n,\\alpha}\\), so the definition of minimax expected maximal width gives\n\\[\n \\mathfrak R_n\n \\le\\sup_{P\\in\\mathcal M}E_{P_{\\mathrm{obs}}^{\\otimes n}}[W_n]\n \\le C r_n.                                                   \\tag{24}\n\\]\nFor the converse, take an arbitrary \\((L_n,U_n)\\in\\mathfrak B_{n,\\alpha}\\) and the two laws supplied by the established fixed-nuisance marked-pair theorem.  Define\n\\[\n A_j=\\{L_n(a)\\le\\mu_{j,n}(a)\\le U_n(a)\n          \\text{ for every }a\\in I\\},\\qquad j\\in\\{0,1\\}.\n\\]\nUniform honesty gives\n\\[\n P_{j,n,\\mathrm{obs}}^{\\otimes n}(A_j)\\ge1-\\alpha.           \\tag{25}\n\\]\nThe total-variation inequality \\(P(B)\\ge Q(B)-\\|P-Q\\|_{\\mathrm{TV}}\\), applied to \\(A_1\\), and the marked-pair bound give\n\\[\n P_{0,n,\\mathrm{obs}}^{\\otimes n}(A_1)\n \\ge1-\\alpha-\\eta.                                          \\tag{26}\n\\]\nBy the union bound, (25)--(26) imply\n\\[\n P_{0,n,\\mathrm{obs}}^{\\otimes n}(A_0\\cap A_1)\n \\ge1-2\\alpha-\\eta>0,                                       \\tag{27}\n\\]\nwhere positivity is exactly the declared restriction \\(\\eta<1-2\\alpha\\).  On \\(A_0\\cap A_1\\), both causal curves are contained pointwise in the same band, so\n\\[\n W_n\\ge\\|\\mu_{1,n}-\\mu_{0,n}\\|_{L^\\infty(I)}\\ge c r_n.     \\tag{28}\n\\]\nTaking expectation under \\(P_{0,n,\\mathrm{obs}}^{\\otimes n}\\), using (27), then taking the supremum over \\(\\mathcal M\\) and infimum over honest bands yields\n\\[\n \\mathfrak R_n\\ge c(1-2\\alpha-\\eta)r_n.                     \\tag{29}\n\\]\nThe constants \\(c_K>0\\) and \\(\\beta>1/2\\) are fixed.  Hence\n\\[\n K_n\\asymp\\frac{\\log n}{\\log\\log n},\n \\qquad\n r_n=K_n^{1/2-\\beta}\n \\asymp\\left\\{\\frac{\\log\\log n}{\\log n}\\right\\}^{\\beta-1/2}. \\tag{30}\n\\]\nCombining (24), (29), and (30) proves both asserted inequalities and the equivalent frontier for the broadened smoothness range.",
